## Outcomes

When this spec is executed:

- Every asset in every category has a populated, varying, in-range `capacity`/`platform_height` — no category still depends on the midpoint fallback as its normal path.
- Each category has **27 assets total** across the fleet (Excavator 7, Fork Lift 6, Scissors Lift 7, Boom Lift 7) — see "Requirements" for the exact per-category shape.
- In every category, **one spec-band holds 4 assets** (real depth — `period_utilization` there can be `0`, `1/4`, `1/2`, `3/4`, or `1`), and **every other spec-band in that category holds exactly 1 asset** (real coverage of the category's full size range, not an empty gap whose behavior depends on a Haystack-side fallback this repo can't verify). No spec-band is left at zero assets; no spec-band other than the deliberate 4-asset one has more than one.
- Each category's assets span all 4 `ConditionType` values.
- Bookings cover all 6 `BookingStatus` values at least once, including `PENDING_DEPOSIT` and `CANCELLED`.
- Every `Booking` row — the existing 20 and every new one — has at least one `BookingItem`.
- Every `Booking` row has `Payment`/`DeliveryRecord`/`ReturnRecord` rows appropriate to its status, per `SPEC-seed-data.md` §6.8–§6.10's pattern, scaled to cover the full ~74–101-row booking set (not just the smaller volume considered in earlier drafts of this spec) — see "Requirements".
- New bookings' dates are generated relative to seed time via the same `CURRENT_DATE ± N` convention already in `data.sql`.
- `asset_categories.name` values are unchanged.
- The two existing-row status corrections are applied; **no existing asset's capacity/height/condition/rate values change** — every existing asset already fits naturally into either the 4-asset band or a filler band for its category (see `design.md` "Target volumes").

