## Scope

### In scope

- 19 new `assets` rows (Excavator +5, Fork Lift +4, Scissors Lift +5, Boom Lift +5) plus backfilling `capacity` on the 6 pre-existing non-forklift assets (all 6 currently `NULL`).
- New `asset_images` rows for the 19 new assets, reusing the existing base64 content of the same-brand, same-category sibling asset — no new photo files.
- Row-level data for `bookings` (~54–81 new, landing at ~74–101 total including the unchanged existing 20), `booking_items` (completeness for both new bookings and the 10 currently-orphaned existing bookings), `payments`/`delivery_records`/`return_records` (completeness for the same full set, per status, at the same scale as the booking volume — see Requirements), and 1–2 more `USER`-role customers.
- A relative/rolling date-generation approach for new booking windows, consistent with `data.sql`'s existing `CURRENT_DATE ± N` convention.
- Two single-column `status` corrections on existing rows (`bookings` id 2, id 6).
- Idempotent upsert seeding, consistent with the existing `ddl-auto=update` + `data.sql` upsert convention.

### Out of scope

- Any change to `asset_categories.name` values or to any entity/column/enum definition.
- Real historical transaction data / Phase 3's blend-and-cutover onto genuine bookings.
- Any Haystack-side code change (category-normalization is `../dynamic-pricing/spec.md`'s concern).
- Front-end/portal seed data.
- **Fixing the underlying date-staleness mechanism** (switching bookings to `ON CONFLICT DO UPDATE`, a scheduled reseed, or similar) — a larger behavioral change not needed to satisfy any acceptance scenario here.
- Any change to the existing 8 assets' `min_daily_rate`/`max_daily_rate`/`base_daily_rate`/`capacity`/`platform_height`/`condition` values (backfilling the 6 `NULL` capacities is the one exception, and even then their target band placement was chosen so no value needs revisiting later), or to any of the original 20 bookings' amounts/dates/customer — other than the two named `status` corrections.
- Code changes to `AssetService`/`EquipmentController` or any other Java class — this spec is data-only.

