## Verification

Run against `primary_snapshot` (or `public`, same content per the sync) after seeding:

```sql
-- capacity nulls: expect 0
select count(*) from assets where capacity is null;

-- asset count: expect 27
select count(*) from assets;

-- condition spread per category: expect 4 for every category
select ac.name, count(distinct a.condition)
from assets a join asset_categories ac on a.category_id = ac.id
group by ac.name;

-- booking status coverage: expect 6
select count(distinct status) from bookings;

-- booking count: expect 74-101
select count(*) from bookings;

-- orphaned bookings: expect 0
select count(*) from bookings b
left join booking_items bi on bi.booking_id = b.id
where bi.id is null;

-- bookings missing a payment row entirely: expect 0
select count(*) from bookings b
left join payments p on p.booking_id = b.id
where p.id is null;

-- MOBILISED/COMPLETED bookings missing a delivery record: expect 0
select count(*) from bookings b
left join delivery_records dr on dr.booking_id = b.id
where b.status in ('MOBILISED','COMPLETED') and dr.id is null;

-- COMPLETED bookings missing a return record: expect 0
select count(*) from bookings b
left join return_records rr on rr.booking_id = b.id
where b.status = 'COMPLETED' and rr.id is null;

-- existing-row corrections
select id, status from bookings where id in (2, 6); -- expect COMPLETED, CANCELLED
```

Plus a `period_utilization` spot-check via `app/repositories/pricing_repository.py`'s `compute_period_utilization()` (once the category-mapping fix lands) for one category's 4-asset spec-band — confirm a fractional, non-0/0.5/1 result (e.g. `1/4`, `2/4`, or `3/4`).

